==Trivia==
*Aka-Jūtan's name was a pun. While 赤絨毯 translates to "Red Carpet", it also sounds like 赤十反 ("Red Ten Bolts"), whereas its base variant's name, [[wikipedia:Ittan-momen|Ittan-Momen]], means "One Bolt of Cotton"; the implied increase of one to ten reflects Aka-Jūtan's increased power compared to the original.
*Yuki-Onna's Dark variant, Yuki-Onna Junjōha, may have been a reference to the song "Roppongi Junjōha" by Yōko Oginome, or to the television drama ''Hagure Keiji Junjōha''.
*鬼女 (oni-woman) would normally be read as ''[[wikipedia:Kijo (folklore)|kijo]]''; it's unknown why the one in this game was read as ''oni-onna''.
*[[Pigge]] and [[Teacher Bun Bun]] had smoother animations than in [[The Battle Cats]], despite still being rendered in the Battle Cats art style.

